@*
    FundMark — the company seal at small sizes.

    This used to be a drawing *of* the seal: a gold ring with a shield inside it,
    reduced to the two moves that survive at 30px. It was legible, but a gold
    ring and a shield is not the logo — it is a generic badge, and next to the
    real seal on the sign-in page it read as a second, unrelated mark.

    So this is the artwork itself, cropped to its disc and served at 128px for
    display sizes in the 30-48px range. The ring lettering is mud down there and
    always will be; what survives is the gold ring, the navy shield and the
    sunburst, which is enough for someone who knows the mark to recognise it.

    There is no vector of this artwork -- it is a rendered illustration, not an
    icon -- so the density of the raster is what keeps it sharp. If a vector
    version ever arrives, this is the one place that has to change.

    The seal's outer band is white, so it does not need a ground: it sits on the
    dark panel and on the paper without a plate behind it. That is why the old
    Ground and Metal parameters are gone rather than kept as no-ops.
*@

@* An empty Label means the mark sits beside words that already name the
   company, so alt="" drops it out of the accessibility tree entirely rather
   than announcing the company twice. *@
<img class="@Class"
     src="img/jte-mark-128.png"
     width="@Size"
     height="@Size"
     alt="@Label"
     draggable="false"
     decoding="async" />

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public int Size { get; set; } = 34;

    [Parameter]
    public string? Class { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Decorative beside a wordmark that already names the company; pass an
    /// empty label there so the name is not announced twice.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Label { get; set; } = "Jiane's Tech";
}
